<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Nuʻuanu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1795</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Nuʻuanu was fought on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oahu">Oʻahu</a> in May 1795, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kamehameha-i">Kamehameha I</a>, armed with Western guns and advisers, defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalanikupule">Kalanikūpule</a>, ruler of Oʻahu and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maui">Maui</a>. Many defenders were driven over the cliffs of the Nuʻuanu Pali. The victory brought Oʻahu under Kamehameha's rule and was decisive in the unification of the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hawaii">Hawaii</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-nuuanu.jpg" alt="Battle of Nuʻuanu" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User:Jiang · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nuuanu_Pali_(1258).JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
